From d0650165983e32adf7b6bdc0442a3599d840a04a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:02:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Battle: touch on the command row, lists, targets and messages

In the touch layout (include/arena/battle_touch.h, short hooks in the
battle menus):
- the command row: a tap selects an icon, a tap on the selected one
  chooses it (Fight, Attack, Psynergy and the rest);
- the Psynergy, Djinn and item lists: a tap selects a row or chooses the
  selected one; the page arrows turn pages;
- the targets: a tap on a unit aims at it, a tap on the aimed one confirms
  (a tap anywhere for an action that takes every unit);
- a Back button (B) by the open menu: above the portrait in a member's
  command row, at the left of the lists and the targets;
- battle messages waiting on the arrow go on with a tap anywhere.
Classic and the GBA build are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ta8ykfbWFo924wEqysLhg
